## SQ-MB-03 | wave dead -> one reward stack, rest phase
# scratch-only: no mob drops, so the item count is the reward alone; bot leaves at once so the 200-tick cooldown
# does not re-arm the box with the bot beside it (SQ-MB-04 needs phase 0 first) and the bot cannot pick up the reward
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item]
> gamerule doMobLoot false
> tp qa 0 -60 0
> execute positioned 20 -60 -20 run kill @e[type=!minecraft:player,type=!minecraft:item,distance=..24]
sleep 3
> data get block 20 -60 -20
> execute positioned 20 -60 -20 if entity @e[type=item,distance=..3]
expect creativeengineering:phase": 2b
expect creativeengineering:until
expect Test passed, count: 1
> gamerule doMobLoot true
look until = game time + 72000 normally; this boot has cooldownTicks 200, so until = game time + 200

